+# Native-busy worker-flight measurement
+
+SOURCE ONLY; interval tests and all new normal/BURN/worker-off/browser execution UNRUN. Base `79cdb85d6ab8a58dde5d474e254cffa027735c51`. No product, threshold, fixture, font or dependency changes.
+
+The original79 Windows YAML quick flight89ms/159ms baseline failure remains RED and its exact cause UNKNOWN: it has no raw timing trace. Two separately accepted passive witnesses preserve the original metric/gates and pass: Mac32.584s and Windows36.839s. Independent analysis exactly recomputes all80samples in each. Both demonstrate an actual measurement boundary defect:20Mac and10Windows winning flight samples include excess outside even the widest native-busy window, with maxima7.3ms and9.5ms respectively. Every such beat end equals the delayed MutationObserver close timestamp numerically; native checking cleared earlier. This establishes the mechanism on both platforms, not the old89ms cause or a product regression.
+
+Retained raw Mac report1263045B SHA256 `ee1abe8c6b7fd2df4d9baf6812aad0c64f6dd2a81efb747ddf99b0454cf5557e`; Windows report1200712B SHA256 `73b883b6596ffe1509187414cf258b4c0c07d7df94288dd6afe4d4a1eabbcad8`. Data/analyses remain `/tmp/opf-worker-flight-diagnostic-run01/report.json`, `/tmp/opf-worker-flight-windows-review01/payload/browser/report.json` and `/tmp/opf-worker-flight-{independent-analysis01,windows-independent-analysis01}/`. No native Office claim is part of either witness. The separate Windows managed-fixture failure is not this browser result.
+
+The corrected flight value is the maximum over EVERY heartbeat interval of min(positive heartbeat excess, union length of possible native-busy time intersected by that interval). Busy boundaries bracket the actual native dataset/remove write with performance.now before/after. The4ms nominal timer period is not invented as blocked time; taking the upper bound assumes as much of the observed excess as possible happened while busy. It is a conservative wall-time attribution, not measured CPU duration. All intersecting beats participate, including those ending after busy clears; this can increase prior flight values, so it is not a cap on old selected winners or a half-open endpoint workaround. Overlapping/adjacent windows form a union without double counting. Invalid/decreasing clocks refuse.
+
+The one-pane test hook delegates DOMStringMap operations with the real native receiver and removeAttribute with its original receiver/arguments/result/throw, then restores original own descriptors. It does not wrap Worker prototypes or change source-pane/product code. It records bounds on full beats/native edges/MO observations/long tasks/sample data; cap overflow/open spans/clock faults/restoration errors refuse completeness. Existing checks, source text,1000slides,4quick/12paced edits, three formats, all modes/rounds/env flags, actual keyboard events, timeouts,40%flight/85%whole-edit/3xlimit ceiling, uppermedian, majority-flight/counts, final text/error checks and original fail-fast ordering stay unchanged. The old MO-derived result remains raw evidence; whole-edit fields are reused exactly. The shared interval function runs in Node after collecting a sample; the extra raw transfer/recording has diagnostic overhead and is not claimed cost-free.
+
+Every run creates a fresh owned `packages/editor/artifacts/source-worker-perf/<timestamp>-<pid>/report.json` before startup; after each measure it captures raw page evidence/restores hooks/persists before page close and verdict gates, then persists again in outer finally. Original assertions survive secondary capture/write/close failures. As before, startKeyboardSuite/openPage startup boundaries rely on normal runner logs for failures that occur before their try blocks; the initial owned report still exists. Source/helper/budget hashes, actual Node/browser/parameters and partial samples are retained. No prior output is overwritten; incomplete evidence cannot turn an original failure green.
+
+The new top-level `worker-flight-intervals.mjs` is discovered by the existing runner; its helper lives under support and is not a top-level runnable test. No package.json/test-list changes. Finite independent cases cover entry/exit/full outside/full inside/multiple union/late endpoints/nominal4ms/invalid clocks plus real retainedMac/Win examples. An actual late-ending Mac beat demonstrates an increase over the old selected maximum. Pure budget-reason controls cover full busy BURN-like refusal, no-request majority refusal and a small busy overlap with large outside-apply time; they do not replace real qualification. Root must run the new normal test and existing actual worker-off/BURN45 negative controls (for intended reasons), plus the applicable unchanged outside-apply positive if needed, after root/peer review. All such execution remains UNRUN here.
